---Imagine you're an HR analyst at a tech company tasked with analyzing employee salaries. Your manager is keen on understanding the pay distribution and asks you to determine the 
second highest salary among all employees.It's possible that multiple employees may share the same second highest salary. 
In case of duplicate, display the salary only once---

WITH HIGHEST_SALARY AS
(SELECT *, RANK() OVER(ORDER BY salary Desc) As rank FROM employee)
 
 SELECT salary FROM HIGHEST_SALARY  WHERE rank=2 ;
